    "id": "all-on-6-en",
    "title": "All-on-6 in Albania: Timeline & Full-Arch Guide for UK Patients",
    "slug": "all-on-6-in-albania-cost-timeline-full-arch-guide-for-uk-pat",
    "category": "dental-tourism",
    "excerpt": "A clear, honest guide to All-on-6 dental implants in Albania, what the treatment costs compared with the UK, and how international patients are cared for at Dental Med Austria in Tirana.",
    "body": "If you are researching All-on-6 in Albania, here is the answer first: a full-arch All-on-6 restoration is delivered to premium standards per arch, using the same brands as in the UK or Ireland. All-on-6 uses six dental implants to anchor a fixed full-arch bridge, giving you a permanently secured set of teeth in one jaw. At Dental Med Austria in Tirana, every figure is confirmed only after a free remote treatment plan, so the number you act on is realistic for your case rather than a headline price.\n\nBelow you will find how All-on-6 works, who genuinely needs six implants, what the treatment trip looks like, and the materials and guarantees behind the treatment.\n\n## What All-on-6 is and how it differs from All-on-4\n\nAll-on-6 is a full-arch dental implant solution that replaces all the teeth in one jaw using six titanium implants to support a single fixed bridge. The \"6\" refers to the number of implants; the bridge itself usually carries 12-14 teeth. It is a fixed restoration, not a removable denture, so it stays in place day and night and is cleaned much like natural teeth.\n\nThe difference from All-on-4 comes down to support and how the bite is distributed. All-on-4 uses four implants and is a well-proven, excellent option, especially when bone is limited. All-on-6 adds two more implants, spreading chewing forces across a wider footprint. For many patients this means greater long-term stability and a more even bite, particularly in the upper jaw where bone tends to be softer. Choosing between full arch 6 implants and a four-implant design is a clinical decision, not a marketing one, and it depends on your bone volume, your bite and your goals. You can see how we approach full-arch cases in our [treatment catalogue](/en/catalogue).\n\n## Who needs six implants\n\nSix implants are not always necessary, and an honest clinic will tell you so. All-on-6 tends to suit patients who have lost most or all of their teeth, have reasonable bone in the back of the jaw, and want the most robust fixed result. It is also frequently recommended for the upper jaw, where the softer bone benefits from the extra anchorage, and for people who clench, grind or simply have a powerful bite.\n\nThe only way to know what is right for you is a 3D assessment. At Dental Med Austria we use a Vatech 3D CBCT scan to measure your bone in detail, then plan each implant position with Navident guided surgery so placement matches the plan precisely. If you do not have enough bone, biomaterials such as Botiss Cerabone and the Jason membrane can rebuild the site rather than ruling treatment out. Send us your existing scan or X-ray and we will tell you, honestly, whether four or six implants serve you best.\n\n## Premium quality in Albania\n\nThe reason patients travel from the UK, Ireland and worldwide is straightforward: Albania offers premium-quality dentistry. All-on-6 in Albania is planned per arch, or for both jaws, depending on the implant brand and final bridge material you choose.\n\nThose numbers are deliberately given as ranges, because your real price depends on your bone, whether grafting is needed, and which materials you select. That is exactly why we never quote a binding figure online. Instead, you receive a free, personalised treatment plan within 24-48 hours that itemises everything, with no obligation. You can also compare bundled options, including hotel and transfers, in our [all-inclusive packages](/en/packets).\n\n## The treatment trip and timeline\n\nFor most patients, All-on-6 in Albania is completed over two trips to Tirana. On the first visit, we carry out the CBCT scan, place the six implants under guided surgery, and fit a fixed temporary bridge so you leave with teeth, never gaps. This stay is usually three to five days.\n\nA healing period of about three to four months follows, during which the implants integrate with the bone. You then return for a second visit of roughly five to seven days to fit your final, custom-milled bridge. Because we run an in-house iMES iCORE CAD/CAM milling unit and a Zeiss operating microscope, much of the precision work happens in one place, which keeps the timeline tight. From the moment you land, our team handles airport pickup in Tirana, partner hotels and multilingual support in English, Italian, German and Albanian, so the logistics never fall on you. The practical details of each visit are explained on our [patient care page](/en/care).\n\n## Materials, stability and the written treatment guarantee\n\nA full arch is only as good as the parts it is built from, so we are specific about ours. For the implants themselves you can choose Straumann BLX, the Swiss-made gold standard, French ETK, Alpha-Bio, or German CE-marked Biodem implants that come with an implant passport. Every implant carries a lifetime manufacturer warranty.\n\nFor the bridge and aesthetics we work with Ivoclar IPS e.max and high-strength zirconia, materials chosen for durability and a natural look. Behind all of this sits a clinic built to European quality standards, certified to ISO 9001, using rigorous sterilisation protocols. Our track record stands at more than 42,000 implants placed with a 98% success rate, and the practice is led by an experienced clinical team. On top of the manufacturer warranties, your treatment is backed by our written treatment guarantee, so your investment is protected long after you fly home.\n\n## Conclusion + free treatment plan\n\nAll-on-6 gives you a fixed, full-arch set of teeth built on six implants, and in Albania it is delivered without compromising on Swiss, German and French components or European standards. The right number of implants, the right materials and an honest timeline can only be confirmed once a clinician has seen your case.\n\nThat assessment is free. Send us your CBCT scan, X-ray or even a few photos, and our clinical team at Dental Med Austria will return a personalised All-on-6 treatment plan within 24-48 hours, with a clear price range and no obligation. [Contact us today](/en/contact) to start your plan and find out exactly what your new smile would involve.",
